Blank build-machine info in numpy __config__ for reproducible builds

The generated numpy/__config__.py records the build machine's cpu and
family (e.g. "x86_64" or "aarch64"), which makes the target image differ
byte-for-byte depending on the architecture of the machine that built it.
Blank the two fields so images are identical regardless of build host.
numpy's _cleanup() drops empty values, so they simply disappear from
numpy.show_config() output; nothing else consumes them.

--- a/numpy/__config__.py.in
+++ b/numpy/__config__.py.in
@@ -57,8 +57,8 @@
                 "system": "@HOST_CPU_SYSTEM@",
             },
             "build": {
-                "cpu": "@BUILD_CPU@",
-                "family": "@BUILD_CPU_FAMILY@",
+                "cpu": "",
+                "family": "",
                 "endian": "@BUILD_CPU_ENDIAN@",
                 "system": "@BUILD_CPU_SYSTEM@",
             },
